From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: keep the HAL when crash recovery fails

Since commit 32be3ca4cf78 ("wifi: ath11k: HAL SRNG: don't deinitialize
and re-initialize again"), crash recovery keeps the HAL across restarts:
ath11k_core_reconfigure_on_crash() only clears it with
ath11k_hal_srng_clear() and no longer calls ath11k_hal_srng_init(). Its
error path still calls ath11k_hal_srng_deinit(), though, which frees
srng_config and the shared rdp/wrp buffers. After a recovery fails, the
next one clears the freed HAL and dereferences the NULL srng_config:

  ath11k_pci 0006:01:00.0: failed to start core: -110
  ath11k_pci 0006:01:00.0: firmware crashed: MHI_CB_EE_RDDM
  ath11k_pci 0006:01:00.0: failed to reconfigure driver on crash recovery
  ...
  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 0000000000000014
  Workqueue: ath11k_wq ath11k_core_restart
  pc : ath11k_hal_srng_shadow_config+0x44/0xa8
  lr : ath11k_ce_get_shadow_config+0x4c/0x100
  Call trace:
   ath11k_hal_srng_shadow_config+0x44/0xa8 (P)
   ath11k_ce_get_shadow_config+0x4c/0x100
   ath11k_core_qmi_firmware_ready+0x84/0x5a4
   ath11k_core_restart+0xb0/0x18c
   process_one_work+0x15c/0x498
   worker_thread+0x18c/0x310
   kthread+0x134/0x140
   ret_from_fork+0x10/0x20

So once a recovery fails, the next firmware crash takes the kernel down.
Keep the HAL on failure as on success: the next recovery clears and
reuses it, and ath11k_pci_remove() frees it.

Tested-on: WCN6855 hw2.1 PCI WLAN.HSP.1.1-03125-QCAHSPSWPL_V1_V2_SILICONZ_LITE-3.6510.41

Fixes: 32be3ca4cf78 ("wifi: ath11k: HAL SRNG: don't deinitialize and re-initialize again")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c | 11 ++++++-----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
index 8dacc87..6e9f10c 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
@@ -2347,17 +2347,18 @@ static int ath11k_core_reconfigure_on_crash(struct ath11k_base *ab)
 
 	clear_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH, &ab->dev_flags);
 
+	/*
+	 * On failure the HAL stays as it is: the next recovery clears and
+	 * reuses it like this one did, and it is freed when the device goes
+	 * away.
+	 */
 	ret = ath11k_core_qmi_firmware_ready(ab);
 	if (ret)
-		goto err_hal_srng_deinit;
+		return ret;
 
 	clear_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_RECOVERY, &ab->dev_flags);
 
 	return 0;
-
-err_hal_srng_deinit:
-	ath11k_hal_srng_deinit(ab);
-	return ret;
 }
 
 void ath11k_core_halt(struct ath11k *ar)
